ARM: dts: rk3126-taq102: the eMMC, the SDIO and the block-device numbering

The board built without these and would have booted to a tablet with no
storage and no Wi-Fi: rk3128.dtsi leaves all three dw_mmc controllers
disabled, and nothing in the series so far enabled them. Without the eMMC
there is no /data, so no settings and no wifi.conf; without the SDIO there is
no wlan0 whatever rtw88 is built with.

Every capability here is the one the tablet's own stock tree sets for this
board: the eMMC is 8-bit, non-removable and high-speed with write protect
disabled; the SDIO is 4-bit, high-speed, non-removable and keeps power in
suspend. The RTL8723CS needs its 32 kHz clock and its reset released before
its SDIO function can be probed, so the power sequence takes the PMIC's
clkout2 and GPIO2_B5, which is why the PMIC node gains a label.

The aliases are not cosmetic. They fix the eMMC at mmcblk1, which is what the
vendor kernel called it, what the blkdevparts= on the command line names, and
what the initramfs looks for when it hunts for the partition at LBA 4867072.
Mainline has no Rockchip partition parser, so that command line is the only
thing that makes /data findable at all.

The SD slot is left disabled deliberately. Nothing here uses it, and enabling
it only adds a controller that can fail to probe.

Verified by decompiling the built DTB: both controllers status okay with the
capabilities above, mmc0/mmc1/mmc2 pointing at sdmmc/emmc/sdio.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3126-taq102.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3126-taq102.dts
@@ -24,6 +24,24 @@
 	model = "Denver TAQ-102 (RK3126C, LVDS)";
 	compatible = "rockchip,rk3126-taq102", "rockchip,rk3126";
 
+	aliases {
+		mmc0 = &sdmmc;
+		mmc1 = &emmc;
+		mmc2 = &sdio;
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The RTL8723CS needs its 32 kHz clock and its reset released before
+	 * the SDIO function can be probed at all. Values from the tablet own
+	 * stock tree: the clock is the PMIC clkout2, the reset is GPIO2_B5.
+	 */
+	sdio_pwrseq: sdio-pwrseq {
+		compatible = "mmc-pwrseq-simple";
+		clocks = <&rk816 1>;
+		clock-names = "ext_clock";
+		reset-gpios = <&gpio2 RK_PB5 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	};
+
 	memory@60000000 {
 		device_type = "memory";
 		reg = <0x60000000 0x40000000>;
@@ -211,7 +229,7 @@
 &i2c2 {
 	status = "okay";
 
-	pmic@1a {
+	rk816: pmic@1a {
 		compatible = "rockchip,rk816";
 		reg = <0x1a>;
 		interrupt-parent = <&gpio0>;
@@ -296,3 +314,32 @@
 				       <3450000 0>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Storage and SDIO. Without the eMMC there is no /data, so no settings and no
+ * wifi.conf; without the SDIO there is no wlan0 whatever rtw88 is built with.
+ * Every capability below is the one the stock tree sets for this board.
+ * The SD slot is left disabled on purpose: nothing here uses it, and it would
+ * only add a controller that can fail to probe.
+ */
+&emmc {
+	bus-width = <8>;
+	cap-mmc-highspeed;
+	disable-wp;
+	non-removable;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&emmc_clk &emmc_cmd &emmc_bus8>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&sdio {
+	bus-width = <4>;
+	cap-sd-highspeed;
+	keep-power-in-suspend;
+	max-frequency = <50000000>;
+	mmc-pwrseq = <&sdio_pwrseq>;
+	non-removable;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&sdio_clk &sdio_cmd &sdio_bus4>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
